The wait for &#x201C;Avengers: Doomsday&#x201D; is almost over, and soon, fans can play in that world in addition to watching the story unfold.

To celebrate the movie hitting theaters Dec. 18, Scopely, in collaboration with Marvel Games, is uniting &#x201C;Monopoly Go!&#x201D; with Marvel Studios&#x2019; highly anticipated &#x201C;Avengers: Doomsday&#x201D; for an all-new season of &#x201C;Doomsday Go!&#x201D;

This season, which runs Nov. 25 - Jan. 27, brings new shields, tokens and dice with richer animations and visual effects and visually enhanced super stickers and super tokens. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Jo Koy on ‘Blue in the Face,’ Steven Spielberg, Biggie’s Mom and Learning What His Name Really Means at Long John Silver’s 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' Extended Cut Sets December Release Date in Theaters

The &#x201C;Doomsday Go!&#x201D; album is packed with 23 unique sticker sets featuring Marvel Super Heroes from Thor and Iron Man to Deadpool, Wolverine, Spider-Man, the X-Men and more. Players can collect super hero team sets, follow story sets, explore whimsical designs and piece together puzzles as Tycoons build a collection worthy of the Marvel Universe.

See more gaming news from the week in the roundup below.

The Battle of the Boroughs Minecraft Competition will return to New York City for the fifth consecutive year.

Hosted by New York City Public Schools and the NYC Mayor's Office of Media and Entertainment (MOME), the competition incentivizes students in grades 3-12 to build a more inclusive and sustainable culture while developing critical thinking, computer science, public speaking and problem-solving skills. This year's prompt will challenge students to develop Minecraft builds that create a safer, more connected Penn Station neighborhood.

Submissions for elementary, middle and high school teams are now open on the New York City Public Schools website and close Jan. 6. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

ITV Studios unveiled on Monday a faithful, nostalgia-packed &#x201C;Roblox&#x201D; experience based on the original 1960s TV series &#x201C;Thunderbirds.&#x201D;

The game introduces a new generation to the series by recreating the look and spirit of the show, from the famous launch sequences to the craft designs fans grew up with, all with a modern twist.

&#x201C;Recreating Thunderbirds, such an iconic piece of British television and a treasured brand at ITV Studios, required immense care, passion and dedication,&#x201D; Ashley Lewis, managing director of Metavision, said. &#x201C;By pairing the unmistakable DNA and enduring spirit of the 1960s original with Roblox&#x2019;s rapidly evolving technical capabilities, we&#x2019;ve been able to bring Tracy Island and its iconic rescues to life with truly impressive scale and fidelity. We hope we&#x2019;ve created an authentic experience for long-standing fans while introducing a new generation to the excitement and imagination of Thunderbirds.&#x201D;

David Fincher admitted in an interview published Wednesday that some AI was used in the post-production of &#x201C; The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth ,&#x201D;&#xA0;but that it was all done to enhance the work of &#x201C;real human beings.&#x201D;

Fincher appeared on The Ringer's &#x201C;Big Picture&#x201D;&#xA0;podcast, where he told host Sean Fennessey that AI helped sync the best take of a line reading with the best performance take when they didn't align on camera. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' Spins Up Massive Numbers for Sony's Quarterly Earnings Brad Pitt Says 'Ocean's 14' Not Shooting Until 'Late' 2027

&#x201C;I feel like with the tools we now have,&#x201D;&#xA0;Fincher said, before adding that the film only spent between four or five days of actors re-recording their dialogue above scenes. Only 5% of the film used &#x201C;automated dialogue replacement, he said, while the rest was &#x201C;all AI.&#x201D;

&#x201C;We could use AI to re-lip that thing,&#x201D;&#xA0;he added. &#x201C;So it was freeing, it was the freeing up of…think of this entirely plastically. We're not chiseling this out of marble. We're working with plasticine. You know what I mean? Just giving ourselves that freedom to go, &#x2018;what is the best thing on the eye, and then what is the best thing on the ear&#x2019; and fucking do not worry about how we're going to get there, because we will figure out a way. And we did, in most cases. I think there's a couple of shots [that] didn't quite work, but they're getting there. By the time it's on service.&#x201D;

Fennessey premised his interview on the podcast by noting it took place before allegations regarding the use of generative AI on the film emerged, so he didn't ask Fincher about other potential instances of AI in the film. Still, Fincher said he viewed AI as a tool that could help creatives focus on the work the technology can't assist with, such as &#x201C;sculpting, painting, aging, blowing fake spiders&#x2019; webs into the corner, smoking up a volume, putting a shaft of light in it&#x201D;&#xA0;or &#x201C;putting [a] crazy f&#x2014;king wig on somebody.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I can imagine a world where, and I don&#x2019;t think we&#x2019;re far away, you hire all the same people,&#x201D; Fincher said. &#x201C;You walk into a set that&#x2019;s beautifully handcrafted and you hire all those people, and you shoot the master. You shoot the master 20, 25 times till you get worked out exactly.&#x201D;

Doing so, he said, can lower the intense amount of takes he's known for, &#x201C;because I won't miss focus in AI. I will land a stick that all they shot in AI. And I will be able to make sure that hair doesn't cross right in front of your cornea in AI.&#x201D;

&#x201C;It'll still be based on real human beings,&#x201D;&#xA0;Fincher added. &#x201C;It'll still be based on real human, the way humans move and how they traverse a set and how they, how they pull up their trousers before they sit down or take their coat off. All that stuff will be there, people will only have to do it 15 times.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Does working that way appeal to you?&#x201D; Fennessey asked.

&#x201C;Totally,&#x201D;&#xA0;Fincher replied.

The comments came days after those who attended early screenings of the Netflix film, out in Imax theaters Wednesday, cited instances where generative AI appeared to have been used, including during a flashback scene where a horse carriage appeared to have two wagons. &#x201C;What could have been a really great sequel is overshadowed by some of the most blatant and egregious AI use I&#x2019;ve ever seen in a studio film,&#x201D;

Fincher and Netflix have not commented on those instances, though he told the Los Angeles Times in an interview published last week that he didn't fear the emergence of AI as a filmmaking tool. &#x201C;It exists. Should we not use it?&#x201D; he said.

&#x201C;Is everyone satisfied that we have figured this art form out enough that what we really need to do is go back to celluloid?&#x201D; Fincher added. &#x201C;How long have people painted? 40,000 years? We&#x2019;re talking about a thing that&#x2019;s a hundred years old and everyone&#x2019;s going, &#x2018;Stop. Pencils down. No more iterating. It&#x2019;s not necessary to have at your fingertips the ability to change the color of that person&#x2019;s eyes.&#x2019;&#x201D;

Netflix has also been a proponent of AI in filmmaking, purchasing Ben Affleck's AI tool startup InterPositive for $587 million in March and revealing in August that more than 300 programs in its catalog have used some level of generative AI this year.

Bowen Yang insists that he didn&#x2019;t know &#x201C;Zio&#x201D; was an antisemitic slur .

In a resurfaced clip from his Las Culturistas podcast, the comedian muttered the term under his breath at the mention of Regina Spektor , the Jewish American singer-songwriter. Yang was responding to a guest, another alleged wit named Edy Modica, who said that Spektor was &#x201C;a little Israel, hard-core.&#x201D; Spektor, who was born in the Soviet Union and immigrated to the United States as a child refugee, has been outspoken in her defense of the Jewish state since the Hamas massacre of Oct. 7, 2023, and given her personal history, is well attuned to left-wing antisemitism . When protestors interrupted one of her concerts last year screaming &#x201C;Free Palestine ,&#x201D; a visibly frustrated Spektor announced to the crowd, &#x201C;The only reason I even speak English is because I came here to escape this shit.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies Takashi Miike's 'Bad Lieutenant: Tokyo' From Neon Gets Early 2027 Release Lifestyle Veruschka, Mesmerizing Supermodel of the 1960s and '70s, Dies at 87

&#x201C;Zio,&#x201D; short for &#x201C;Zionist,&#x201D; was popularized by former KKK Grand Wizard David Duke when he was going through a respectability phase and needed a way to attack Jews without actually naming them as such. In his apology, Yang seemed sincerely shocked to hear this. &#x201C;I want to genuinely apologize for using a word on the podcast without knowing its antisemitic history,&#x201D; he wrote on Instagram. &#x201C;Particularly upsetting to realize that I adopted language popularized by far-right movements whose rhetoric we should be wary of and act against.&#x201D;

We should take Yang at his word that he didn&#x2019;t know the antisemitic etymology of &#x201C;Zio.&#x201D; Why would he? So profoundly antisemitic are the progressive cultural spaces Yang inhabits that people toss around racial slurs propagated by men in white hoods without a second thought. Does anyone really believe that Bowen Yang knows the first thing about the Israeli-Palestinian conflict? Like everyone in his social set, one that dominates large swaths of the entertainment world, he acquires his progressive worldview &#x2014; to which vicious hatred of Israel is central &#x2014; by osmosis. If there&#x2019;s one issue that unites the far left and the far right in this country, it&#x2019;s the Jewish Question. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Yang seemed more distraught about the far-right origins of &#x201C;Zio&#x201D; than he did about the community the word intends to harm: Zionists, i.e. anyone who believes in the right of Israel to exist, i.e. the vast majority of the world&#x2019;s Jews. In the minds of Yang and others of his ilk, progressives cannot be antisemitic, just as they cannot be anti-black, anti-woman, anti-gay, or anti-anybody. Bigotry, to them, is exclusively a right-wing phenomenon. Yang isn&#x2019;t an antisemite, you see, he&#x2019;s just an &#x201C;anti-Zionist.&#x201D; We know this because he ended his apology with the requisite &#x201C;Free Palestine,&#x201D; no expression of contrition over Jewish pain complete today without a nod to the movement that wants to eliminate the world&#x2019;s only Jewish state.

Sadly, Yang wasn&#x2019;t the only celebrity to make an antisemitic outburst last week. Like Yang, who owes his career to a Jew (Lorne Michaels), Mark Ruffalo has become a very rich man playing a comic book character created by one (Stan Lee). That didn&#x2019;t stop him from impugning the loyalty of the country&#x2019;s highest ranking Jewish public official. &#x201C;Israel is just one issue in a whole host of reasons Van Hollen is the right leader for our times,&#x201D; Ruffalo tweeted in a post explaining his support for Maryland Senator Chris Van Hollen becoming Senate Majority Leader over Chuck Schumer. &#x201C;We need justice, we need leadership that follows the will of the people not entrenched religious beliefs and loyalties.&#x201D;

Schumer, in other words, cannot be trusted in a position of political leadership because he&#x2019;s a Jew who cares about Israel, a class of Americans whose &#x201C;loyalties&#x201D; are suspect. Ruffalo subjects no other ethnic group to this scrutiny, just Jews. According to him, Schumer is less American that the guy with a &#x201C;Van&#x201D; in his surname. Again, this is the sort of stuff Gregory Peck&#x2019;s character might have encountered in Gentlemen&#x2019;s Agreement coming out of the mouth of a leading Hollywood liberal in the year 2026. At least David Duke has the courage to be forthright in his antisemitism. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

William Goldman&#x2019;s famous maxim about Hollywood &#x2014; &#x201C;nobody knows anything&#x201D; &#x2014; applies just as much, if not more, to its denizens&#x2019; understanding of politics. It is amazing to me, after the popularity of Team America: World Police , Ricky Gervais&#x2019; numerous award show appearances and the Kamala Harris presidential campaign, that celebrities still have the nerve to opine about anything other than filmmaking and whatever gambling platform they&#x2019;re being paid to promote. Does nepo baby Hannah Einbinder realize how ridiculous she sounds, ranting &#x201C;never again for anyone&#x201D; at a gay rights event in support of an Islamist political movement that murders homosexuals and uses rape as a weapon of war? Just as we don&#x2019;t ask plumbers to clean our teeth, we shouldn&#x2019;t rely on people who pretend for a living to inform my political views.

That antisemitism is so rife in certain sectors of Hollywood &#x2014; that stars can so casually invoke hoary old prejudices against Jews and not have to worry for their careers in the way they certainly would were they to slander any other minority &#x2014; says two things about the entertainment industry. One: that while Hollywood was largely built by Jews (something the Academy Museum needed to be prodded into acknowledging ), it is certainly not controlled by them. And two: that in its understanding of prejudice, antisemitism is taken less seriously than other forms of bigotry.

A tale of two Academy Awards ceremonies illustrates how far Hollywood has fallen in this regard. In 1978, the actress Vanessa Redgrave won an Oscar for her role in Julia , based on a book by the Stalinist writer Lillian Hellman. Standing outside the Dorothy Chandler Pavilion were members of the extremist Jewish Defense League protesting Redgrave over her advocacy for the Palestinian cause. Accepting her prize, Redgrave condemned the &#x201C;Zionist hoodlums&#x201D; outside, &#x201C;whose behavior is an insult to the stature of Jews all over the world and to their great and heroic record of struggle against fascism and oppression.&#x201D; The Good Jews, according to Redgrave, are those who fight her political battles. Bad ones support Israel. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Redgrave was appropriately booed. But the real rebuke arrived when the director and screenwriter Paddy Chayefsky later took the stage to present an award. An actual veteran of the war against fascism and a vocal opponent of the Hollywood blacklist, Chayefsky had the bona fides to censure Redgrave for attempting to hijack the evening. &#x201C;I'm sick and tired of people exploiting the occasion of the Academy Awards for the propagation of their own political propaganda,&#x201D; he said, a line that could be uttered at every Oscar ceremony. &#x201C;I would like to suggest to Miss Redgrave that her winning an Academy Award is not a pivotal moment in history, does not require a proclamation and a simple thank you would have sufficed.&#x201D;

Fast forward to 2024, when the director Jonathan Glazer accepted the Oscar for best international film , The Zone of Interest . After thanking the Auschwitz-Birkenau State Museum, Glazer, his two fellow Jewish co-producers behind him, declared, &#x201C;Right now, we stand here as men who refute their Jewishness and the Holocaust being hijacked by an occupation which has led to conflict for so many innocent people.&#x201D; Those grubby Jews, exploiting the Holocaust to perpetrate their own genocide.

This time, however, Glazer was applauded for his appalling remarks. And when Steven Spielberg &#x2014; director of Schindler&#x2019;s List , founder of the Shoah Foundation, and one of the most powerful men in Hollywood &#x2014; took the stage later in the evening, he said nothing. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

There are many ways to measure Hollywood&#x2019;s decline. The lackluster quality of the films. The fall in theatrical attendance. The rise in algorithmic-inspired content. Here&#x2019;s another: the deprecation and marginalization of the people whose creativity helped make it the envy of the world.

James Kirchick is the author of Secret City: The Hidden History of Gay Washington.

Mahershala Ali and Mara Brock Akil were among the honorary award winners at the BlackStar Projects' Luminary Gala, which returned for its fourth edition on November 20 at The Bellevue Hotel in Philadelphia.

Cinematographer John Simmons and Stanley Nelson and Marcia Smith&#x2019;s Firelight Media were also among those honored with career awards on the evening.

BlackStar Projects, the parent organization of the BlackStar Film Festival , hosts the gala, which also serves as a fundraiser for the film festival. The BlackStar Film Festival celebrated its 15th anniversary in August. Previous honorees include Mira Nair, Menelik Shabazz, Ava DuVernay, Julie Dash, Autumn Durald Arkapaw, and Wu-Tang&#x2019;s RZA. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Caron Creighton On Capturing The Fight To Save Northern California's Largest Homeless Encampment With Her Debut Feature 'Wood Street' News Haile Gerima Dissects His 10 Hour Documentary Feature 'Black Lions - Roman Wolves' & Teases His Next Project On America's Black Maroons

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s really incredible to be here with you at our fourth annual Luminary Gala and in the BlackStar Film Festival&#x2019;s 15th year,&#x201D; Maori Karmael Holmes, founder, chief executive, and artistic officer of BlackStar Projects, said as she opened the evening&#x2019;s festivities. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

&#x201C;Back in 2012, we were all volunteers trying to put together a one-time event to celebrate the best of Black cinema from around the world. I couldn&#x2019;t have imagined being here in 2026, in front of such illustrious guests, with BlackStar producing not only the festival, but also our print journal, an annual seminar at Stanford, and dozens of year-round screenings&#x2014;all led by a truly brilliant staff.&#x201D;

Ali, who arrived at the gala fresh off the global rollout of his latest feature, Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother, also reminisced on the early iterations of the BlackStar Film Festival as he took the stage to receive his honorary award. Ali was introduced by Andr&#xE9; Holland.

&#x201C;I&#x2019;m moved to tears. BlackStar, Maori Holmes&#x2014;thank you for having me. It&#x2019;s an honor to be here,&#x201D; Ali began. &#x201C;I got to visit years ago, in 2014, and witness the festival in its early years. It was amazing then, so I can&#x2019;t imagine what it&#x2019;s like now.&#x201D;

Ali continued, telling the audience that he arrived at the gala asking himself, &#x201C;How did I get to a place where someone would feel I was worthy of this kind of love and honor?&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I kept going back to my own luminaries, and one in particular: my grandmother. She&#x2019;s 92, and she&#x2019;s the light in my eyes. She&#x2019;s like my best friend,&#x201D; Ali said, before emotionally recalling how his grandmother helped instill confidence in him as a young kid growing up in Hayward, California.

&#x201C;She&#x2019;d have me repeat after her: I&#x2019;m handsome. I&#x2019;m intelligent. I can do anything I put my mind to. I can be anything I want to be,&#x201D; Ali recalled.

Ali said his grandmother was also one of the first supporters of his decision to pursue acting.

&#x201C;This was 30 years ago, almost to the day. I was working at a record industry magazine for minimum wage, which was about $4.50 an hour at the time. I was trying to figure out what I was doing with my life,&#x201D; Ali said. &#x201C;After spending the summer at the California Shakespeare Festival, I knew passionately that I wanted a shot at acting. I was auditioning for NYU, and I&#x2019;d told my grandparents many times that they only accept about 18 kids from around the country, so pray for me.&#x201D;

One day before his NYU audition, Ali said, his grandmother returned from the grocery store with bundles of sweats and jumpers.

&#x201C;I said, What are those for? She said, You&#x2019;re going to need these when you move to New York,' Ali recalled.

&#x201C;She has been my light. I&#x2019;m so grateful to my mother, of course, but my grandmother&#x2014;what she&#x2019;s done for me over my 50-some-odd years on this earth is guide me to have real belief in myself and my God-given talents,&#x201D; he said.

&#x201C;She taught me to try to be of service to others and to something larger than myself, to try to be a generous actor every day, and to want for others what I want for myself. I try to embody those things. They all come from the best grandmother in the world, Mamie Gilmore.&#x201D;

Fireflight CEO Loira Limbal and Rafiah Vitalis, the company&#x2019;s Senior Director of Finance and Operations, accepted the honorary award on stage for Nelson and Smith, who were also in attendance.

The company is a nonprofit organization that supports, resources, and advocates on behalf of documentary filmmakers of color. Fireflight is best known for its Documentary Lab . Accepting the honorary award, Limbal and Vitalis paid tribute to Nelson and Smith.

&#x201C;26 years ago, our co-founders sat down with the simple, stubborn idea that the stories of our communities deserve to be told by filmmakers from those communities and those filmmakers deserve support, mentorship, and a place to build,&#x201D; Vitalis said. &#x201C;Everything we are is thanks to you two.&#x201D;

Limbal and Vitalis said Fireflight was born out of a long tradition of socially conscious Black and Indigenous non-fiction filmmaking.

&#x201C;Our work is to carry that tradition forward, not as a tribute or memory, but as a continuation,&#x201D; Vitalis said, adding, in union with Limbal: &#x201C;To every filmmaker in this room, keep holding the camera, keep framing the questions, keep the archive.&#x201D;

Next up on the BlackStar calendar is the Greaves Seminar, a symposium for Black, Brown, and Indigenous film artists at Stanford. The seventh edition of the seminar takes place from March 5-7, 2027.

