" Twilight " director Catherine Hardwicke appeared on "The Kyle Buchanan Show" and weighed in on Robert Pattinson 's buzzy casting as the new James Bond actor. Hardwicke is largely responsible for shooting Pattinson's career into the stratosphere by casting him as the vampire Edward Cullen opposite Kristen Stewart as Bella Swan in 2008's "Twilight." Flash forward nearly 20 years and Pattinson is now set to become the movie's most iconic secret agent. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"I almost fell out of my bad," Hardwicke said about the moment she found out about Pattinson's Bond casting. "I just didn't think they were going to choose him because of the Batman and he's so famous and they like to get the unknown [actor]. I did almost fall out of the bed, and that is the same bed that Rob and Kristen auditioned for the first time and did their kissing scene. It was kind of bizarre. He fell out of the best and landed on the floor, so it was kind of cool." Related Stories Daniel Radcliffe Is Unsure If He'll Watch HBO’s ‘Harry Potter’ and Says the New Star ‘Doesn’t Need Any Advice From Me’ 'Adolescence' Writer Jack Thorne Adapts Matt Haig’s 'The Humans' for London’s West End With 'House of the Dragon' Star Matt Smith

Hardwicke added, "He's intense and interesting and has got a lot of stuff going on in there. He's weird and he's original. He does not fit the mold. He's not afraid to say crazy shit, that's what I love about it."

Pattinson and Stewart auditioned for "Twilight" together at Hardwicke's home, where the director was interested to see whether or not the actors had the kind of instant chemistry that was required for Edward and Bella.

