When Lance Oppenheim first told his buddy Nathan Fielder that he heard about the potential to make a new documentary about Elizabeth Holmes&#x2019; last days before going to prison, Fielder wasn&#x2019;t sure what tale there was left to tell. There were other docs, books and an Emmy-winning Hulu series out there about her. &#x201C;I was interested in her, but I didn't really think there was a story there to do, especially for a doc,&#x201D; Fielder said last month from the SCAD Savannah Film Festival , where he and Oppenheim joined The Hollywood Reporter for a special post-screening live Q&A (watch it in full below). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies 'You Can See Everything' Now Streaming: Where to Watch Nathan Fielder's Elizabeth Holmes Doc Online SCAD Savannah Film Festival David Greaves Says 'Once Upon a Time in Harlem' Is "An Act of Resistance" Against Efforts to Erase Black History

Oppenheim remembered Fielder asking, &#x201C;Hasn't there been a billion things made about this person already?&#x201D; And he replied, &#x201C;Yes &#x2014; but maybe there's something else.&#x201D;

To say that has proven true would be the understatement of this film season. Moving in with Holmes and her partner, Billy Evans , in her final weeks of freedom &#x2014; then continuing to make their movie in increasingly daring and surprising directions &#x2014; Oppenheim and Fielder teamed up for You Can See Everything , one of the most successful theatrical documentaries of all time and a bona fide cultural phenomenon.

The movie offers compellingly slippery portraits of both Holmes and Evans, plays off Fielder&#x2019;s noted screen persona to fascinating effect and features a plum secret role for Amanda Seyfried, who won awards for her portrayal of Holmes in The Dropout (and is now a wildcard Oscar contender). But perhaps most fundamentally, it&#x2019;s a singular synthesis of what Fielder and Oppenheim have brought to their work over their last several years, toying with true-story formats in projects as diverse as Primetime and The Rehearsal . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I feel like the two of us are both interested in the challenges of capturing authentic life on camera,&#x201D; Oppenheim said. &#x201C;He's coming at it from a different angle, and I'm coming at it from a different angle too.&#x201D;

Their SCAD Docs to Watch conversation finds the two directors going in-depth on their process from beginning to end on You Can See Everything &#x2014; including the conversations that led to Seyfried&#x2019;s participation and the biggest questions they&#x2019;re still wrestling with, months after completing the movie.

Indeed, the movie has left most every viewer with questions. This dynamic was what motivated Fielder and Oppenheim to make the movie in the first place &#x2014; after only a bit of time spent with Holmes and Evans, it was clear the surreal nature of the arrangement was too rich to ignore.

&#x201C;There were these moments that would happen in the house that we would all witness with our eyes, but when we talked about it at the end of the day, Lance and I would have vastly different ideas of what was actually happening and what was going on &#x2014; and then we talked to the rest of the crew and everyone had different ideas about that,&#x201D; Fielder said. &#x201C;It was then that we were like, &#x2018;Wow, if we can't all agree on this, maybe there's something to this idea.&#x2019;&#x201D;

